// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 2 (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P6): the same LOCAL text pushed twice into a
// LOCAL list of text -- the purely-local shape of the same class C1's
// fixtures cover for globals. Originally (4e): `p6L` (fresh init, only ever
// a push receiver) qualified for a scope-exit element-free loop, but that
// loop would free `p6X`'s handle twice, once per element slot: SIGSEGV at
// handler scope exit. The 4e/pre-ARC fix (`lowEscapeWalkMethodCall`: a
// push/add/unshift value that fails `lowEscapeFreshInit` disqualifies the
// receiver too) disqualified `p6L`'s DEEP release the first time `p6X` --
// a bare identifier, never fresh -- was pushed. Expected 4e/ARC-Task-4 leak
// count: 2 -- `p6X`'s text only (struct box + data handle; `p6X` itself was
// `lowFreeUnsafe`, a push argument, skipped entirely at scope exit; `p6L`'s
// own list handle got only a shallow release, deep still gated on the
// double-free risk).
//
// ARC Task 5 (counted container element slots) closes this fixture to
// ZERO. Every push now retains its non-birth value first (`p6X` is a bare
// identifier, non-birth) -- confirmed against the emitted C: two
// `rt_text_retain`s, one per `p6L.push(p6X)` site, giving rc==3 (`p6X`'s
// own +1 plus one retain per push). Task 5 DELETED the "non-fresh-push
// disqualifies the receiver" consult, so `p6L` now qualifies for a real
// DEEP scope-exit release (confirmed: `{ int32_t i; for (...)
// rt_text_release(*(rt_text **)rt_list_at(cv_p6L, i)); }
// rt_list_release(cv_p6L);`, walking BOTH slots -- rc 3 -> 2 -> 1). Task 5
// also moved push's own value argument off `lowFreeUnsafe` onto shallow-
// safe handoff (`lowEscapeWalkArgsSafeHandoff`) -- `p6X` itself now gets a
// real shallow release too (confirmed: `rt_text_release(cv_p6X);`, rc 1 ->
// 0, the release that finally disposes the box). Three releases (two
// element-walk, one local scope-exit) exactly balance the three owners: no
// leak, no double-free.

func runP6DupPushLocal() {
    var p6L: list of text
    var p6X: text = "dup"
    p6L.push(p6X)
    p6L.push(p6X)
    alert("p6 done")
}
